.TH TORGHOSTNG 1 "@DATE@" "TorGhostNG @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
torghostng \- route traffic through the Tor network
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B torghostng
.RI [ option ]
.RI [ ARG ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B TorGhostNG
redirects TCP traffic through the Tor network using the SOCKS5 proxy on
port 9050, routes DNS resolution through Tor, and optionally restricts
the exit node to a chosen country.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-start " [" EXIT_NODE ]
Start the Tor proxy. Optional EXIT_NODE is a 2-letter ISO country code
(e.g.\ DE, US). Changes are rolled back automatically if startup fails
or is interrupted.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-stop
Stop the proxy and restore system settings (iptables chain, resolv.conf,
torrc, IPv6).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-renew
Send SIGHUP to the Tor daemon to request a fresh circuit.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-check
Verify the Tor connection and print the current exit IP.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage information.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/tor/torrc
Edited at runtime; managed changes are marked with TORGHOSTNG-CONFIG
comments and removed on stop.
.TP
.I /etc/resolv.conf
Backed up and restored when the proxy is active.
.SH NOTES
Must be run as root for network configuration changes.
